  "notes": "Cash-basis county, governmental funds only. Receipts/disbursements from Statement of Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances - Governmental Funds (trimmed p4), Total Governmental Funds column. Taxes 1,932,716 split into property 1,749,478 and motor vehicle 183,238 using the Statement of Activities (p2); they add to the printed line. Beginning cash is the fund balance as originally stated 9,696,519 with the prior period adjustment 120,627 in adjustments (restated 9,817,146). Ending cash = ending fund balance 10,287,835 (cash 9,476,085 plus restricted cash 811,750). Transfers in and out both 1,304,206 (General to Road); they net to zero in the total column; sale of surplus 3,842 in other_financing. Identity: 9,696,519 + 4,350,150 - 3,883,303 + 1,304,206 - 1,304,206 + 3,842 + 120,627 = 10,287,835. Balance sheet is the cash-basis Statement of Net Position (p1); no liabilities. Detail: General Fund uses the budget schedule (p8; more detailed than combining statement p5 for disbursements); its department lines total 1,874,563 but function split differs from statements (e.g. General government departments sum 1,160,500 vs 1,111,578 on p4, reclassifications). General Fund budget schedule excludes the Inheritance Tax Fund, recorded separately from p5 (277,662). Nonmajor funds (12 columns) recorded using Total Non-Major column p7. Road fund budget-basis local 9,244 includes the 3,842 sale of surplus. Transfer cross-check: General transfers out 1,304,206 matches Road transfers in 1,304,206; none hidden in spending. Pages 1-10 only exist in trimmed PDF (original 37). Read pages 1-10 of 10"
}
